nodes.definition:
What it is. Most papers describe Omni-MATH as a mathematics or mathematical reasoning benchmark with diverse topics and a broad range of difficulty, often emphasizing Olympiad-level or olympiad-style problems. A smaller line of work frames it more specifically as a benchmark focused on mathematical olympiad challenges. Some evaluation setups use sampled versions of the benchmark, including Omni-MATH-500 or a random subset of the full dataset, for efficient assessment.

What it is claimed to measure. Across papers, Omni-MATH is linked to two constructs and one behavioral indicator. The prevailing usage is to measure mathematical reasoning, with several papers evaluating models on Omni-MATH as a math reasoning benchmark. A smaller line of work reports it as measuring complex reasoning and problem solving capability, so the measurement claims are concentrated on mathematical reasoning rather than spread widely across many targets.

Space of uses. Papers commonly use Omni-MATH alongside GSM8K, MATH, AIME, OlympiadBench, and GPQA in broader reasoning evaluations. It is usually positioned as one benchmark within multi-benchmark suites, often as a challenging or Olympiad-level component;

What it is. Across the papers, the prevailing framing is a benchmark or dataset for evaluating summary quality in text summarization. Most descriptions present human ratings on four dimensions, fluency, coherence, consistency, and relevance, typically with Likert scores from 1 to 5; one description further specifies news articles and summaries, and one paper specifies 1,600 samples annotated by three human raters. A smaller use treats it mainly as an existing benchmark for comparison on data size and critique dimensions.

What it is claimed to measure. Papers use SummEval to measure text summarization, which is the only linked behavioral indicator, and no constructs are linked to it. Across the linked claims, it is attached to a single behavioral indicator rather than spread across multiple constructs, and the evaluation itself is described in terms of summary quality on fluency, coherence, consistency, and relevance.

Space of uses. No measurement instrument is linked to it. Papers most commonly position it as a summarization benchmark, sometimes alongside DialSumm, and one paper discusses it with NEWSROOM and HANNA as datasets for evaluating text in terms of high-level concepts;
